From: AROS eza port maintainers
Date: 2026-10-21
Subject: [PATCH] Return failure when directory enumeration fails
Repository: eza
Base-Commit: 98442ab17c2c3738701b62a7e060b1431ae2d6ea
Preceding-Patches: 0001-aros-platform.patch
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: all platforms; preserves eza's existing runtime/permission error codes.

A directory can have readable metadata but fail enumeration. print_dirs logged
that failure while returning success, including on an AROS exclusive DOS lock.
Carry the error status through this directory, recursive calls and tree-rendered
child errors, preserving
an earlier nonzero status. No upstream submission has been made.

Verification: host regression observed return0 instead of runtime error1 before
fix; the regression and full no-Git host suite are run with this patch. Native
locked-directory validation is required on the final candidate archive.
Removal: drop once an upstream release includes the same status propagation.

